   "evidence": "`upstream/Physlib/PhyslibAlpha/QuantumMechanics/AngularMomentum/SelectionRules.lean:68`: `def TriangleRule (k m p : \u2115) : Prop := p \u2264 k + m \u2227 k \u2264 m + p \u2227 m \u2264 k + p \u2227 (k + m + p) % 2 = 0` \u2014 the fourth conjunct needs only an even sum. `roadmap/EpsilonEridaniRoadmaps/LightNuclei/README.md:689-693` (\"The three-nucleon bound state is decomposed into the channels of definite total spin, total orbital angular momentum\"). No `triangleRule_iff`-style lemma exists upstream (grep for `TriangleRule` in `upstream/Physlib` returns only the definition, `exists_eq_iff_triangleRule`, `IsTensorOperator.triangleRule`, `IsAllowedMultipole`).",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QuantumMechanics/AngularMomentum/SelectionRulesExtensions.lean",
   "fix": "State `theorem triangleRule_iff_of_even {k m p : \u2115} (h : (k + m + p) % 2 = 0) : TriangleRule k m p \u2194 p \u2264 k + m \u2227 k \u2264 m + p \u2227 m \u2264 k + p` (same `unfold TriangleRule; omega` proof) and either derive the `2 *` form from it or use it directly in `Channel.lean`'s three projections with the side condition by `omega`.",
   "issue": "`triangleRule_two_mul_iff` is stated only for `TriangleRule (2*a) (2*b) (2*c)`, i.e. three integral momenta. The parity conjunct of `TriangleRule` is discharged by evenness of `k + m + p`, not by all three being even, so the natural statement is the general one. The restriction already excludes a case this roadmap needs: \u00a73.1 (three-nucleon channel decomposition) couples half-integral `S` and `J` with integral `L`, where the doubled triple is (odd, even, odd) \u2014 even sum, but not of the form `2*a, 2*b, 2*c`, so this lemma does not apply.",
   "line": 26
  }
 ],
